Write a bash script using AWS CLI (region eu-west-2) and jq that: 1) lists all CloudWatch log groups whose names start with /dna/dtp02, handling pagination; 2) for each log group, runs a CloudWatch Logs Insights query over the last 3 days that filters @message with the case-insensitive regex (passw|pwd|j_password|secret|token|authorization|bindpassword|userpassword) and returns @timestamp and @message (limit 50 per log group); 3) polls each query until it is Complete, Failed or Cancelled, and handles throttling with retries; 4) replaces any value following =, : or a space after the matched keyword with **** before saving, so no real passwords are written out; 5) writes a CSV report with columns: log group, match count, timestamp, masked message; 6) prints a summary of log groups with matches and their counts. Skip log groups with no matches, log any errors without stopping the script, and use set -uo pipefail.
